            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 23 changed paths for security, data exposure and unsafe input handling. I found no reachable exploit.",
              "The PostToolUse decoder in engine/hookwire/posttooluse.go caps total input at 64 MiB. It streams tool_response into a hash and never stores it. It caps the other fields at the 1 MiB envelope bound and the nesting depth at 10000. Oversized or malformed input ends in silence.",
              "The record keeps only the SHA-256 and byte length of the response, so no response content reaches disk. engine/projection/evidence.go sanitizes and bounds the call and session ids, which stops log injection.",
              "OpenAppendNoFollow in engine/statestore/statestore_unix.go keeps O_NOFOLLOW and O_NONBLOCK and now refuses non-regular files. The new tests cover a FIFO, a directory and a symlinked directory. Opening read-write only lets the tail-byte check use the same descriptor.",
              "The torn-line repair in engine/projection/evidencelog/log.go reads the last byte through the open descriptor under the existing lock, so it opens no path race."
            ]
          }
        }
      },
