            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "I read all 23 changed paths and found no concrete resilience failure that this change causes.",
              "The PostToolUse decoder in engine/hookwire/posttooluse.go reads the input in one pass. It hashes tool_response through a 32 KiB buffer and caps the other fields at the 1 MiB envelope bound. Malformed or oversized input ends in silence, and the hook still exits 0.",
              "A failed evidence write returns one additionalContext warning and the hook still exits 0 (engine/cmd/projection_hook.go, postToolUse). Tests cover a directory sitting at the sidecar path.",
              "engine/projection/evidencelog/log.go checks through the locked descriptor whether the file ends in a torn line, so one broken record does not corrupt the next. engine/statestore/statestore_unix.go refuses a FIFO or device without blocking.",
              "Minor, below the reporting bar: the decoder handles each byte through ReadByte and put, so a 64 MiB response costs some CPU. The input is bounded, so I did not report it. OpenAppendNoFollow now opens with O_RDWR, which would fail on a file that is write-only. I saw no realistic case where that happens."
            ]
          }
        }
