            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R2-handwritten-json-scanner",
                "lens": "readability",
                "location": "engine/hookwire/posttooluse.go:91-537",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "The change replaces the standard json.Decoder token loop with a roughly 400-line hand-written JSON scanner (splitter, composite, text, escape, number, digits, literal, sink). It re-implements JSON grammar byte by byte, including number and escape rules and nesting depth. This is a high-complexity, hard-to-audit surface, and any divergence from encoding/json is a latent defect. The sink type also has two modes (hash-through-writer versus keep-in-buffer) selected by whether w is nil, and put() branches on that, which obscures its behavior. The tests cover many cases, but the parser's size and the double-mode sink make later maintenance risky.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/hookwire/posttooluse.go:91-537",
                  "engine/hookwire/posttooluse_test.go:78-177"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              },
              {
                "id": "R2-sink-put-bytewise",
                "lens": "readability",
                "location": "engine/hookwire/posttooluse.go:495-537",
                "severity": "SUGGESTION",
                "claim": "sink.put is called once per byte and checks its mode on every call. The limit logic compares against k.n while buf is reused after flush, so n and len(buf) mean different things in the two modes. A comment on the invariant would help future readers. The ErrTooLarge size argument is also computed as int(k.n)+1, which is easy to misread.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/hookwire/posttooluse.go:495-537"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 23 manifest paths from the full patches.",
              "The main readability risk is the hand-written JSON scanner in engine/hookwire/posttooluse.go. The rest of the change is well commented: the ADR, README, usage text and task notes explain the new behavior and why call_id and session are named as they are.",
              "No BLOCKER or CRITICAL readability defect was found. The new evidence log, the torn-line handling and the statestore regular-file check are each small and documented."
            ]
